## Change 1 hour to seconds
1 \text{ hour} &= 60 \times 60 = 3600 \text{ s}
## Change 120 miles to kilometres
120 \times 1.6 &= 192
So the falcon travels $192$ km in $3600$ s.
## Change kilometres to metres
192 \text{ km} &= 192 \times 1000
&= 192\,000 \text{ m}
## Find the time for 1 metre
$192\,000$ m takes $3600$ s.
\text{Time for 1 m} &= \frac{3600}{192000}
&= 0.01875 \text{ s}
## Find the time for 100 metres
\text{Time for 100 m} &= 100 \times 0.01875
&= 1.875 \text{ s}
&\approx 1.9 \text{ s}
ANSWER: 1.9 \text{ seconds}

## Read the coordinates of A and C
From the diagram, $A = (-2, 0)$ and $C = (0, 3)$.
## Substitute into the slope formula
m_{AC} &= \frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}
m_{AC} &= \frac{3 - 0}{0 - (-2)}
&= \frac{3}{0 + 2}
&= \frac{3}{2}
ANSWER: m_{AC} = \frac{3}{2}

## Find the slope of BC
From the diagram, $B = (5, 0)$ and $C = (0, 3)$.
m_{BC} &= \frac{3 - 0}{0 - 5}
&= \frac{3}{-5}
&= -\frac{3}{5}
## Multiply the two slopes
Two lines are perpendicular only if the product of their slopes is $-1$.
m_{AC} \times m_{BC} &= \frac{3}{2} \times \left(-\frac{3}{5}\right)
&= -\frac{9}{10}
## Compare with $-1$ and tick the box
Since $-\frac{9}{10} \ne -1$, the lines are not perpendicular.
Tick the box: AC is not perpendicular to BC.
ANSWER: AC \text{ is not perpendicular to } BC

## Add the numbers and divide by 7
\text{Mean} &= \frac{17 + 8 + 9 + 8 + 14 + 11 + 28}{7}
&= \frac{95}{7}
&\approx 13.6
ANSWER: 13.6

## Find the range
Range = largest value $-$ smallest value.
\text{Range} &= 113 - 82
&= 31
## Find the mean
\bar{x} &= \frac{104 + 82 + 94 + 113 + 98 + 105}{6}
&= \frac{596}{6}
&= \frac{298}{3}
## Substitute into the standard deviation formula
$\sigma = \sqrt{\dfrac{\sum (x - \bar{x})^2}{n}}$ with $n = 6$. You can also read $\sigma$ straight from a calculator.
\sigma &= \sqrt{\frac{(104 - \bar{x})^2 + (82 - \bar{x})^2 + (94 - \bar{x})^2 + (113 - \bar{x})^2 + (98 - \bar{x})^2 + (105 - \bar{x})^2}{6}}
&= \sqrt{\frac{\left(\frac{14}{3}\right)^2 + \left(-\frac{52}{3}\right)^2 + \left(-\frac{16}{3}\right)^2 + \left(\frac{41}{3}\right)^2 + \left(-\frac{4}{3}\right)^2 + \left(\frac{17}{3}\right)^2}{6}}
&= \sqrt{\frac{\frac{196}{9} + \frac{2704}{9} + \frac{256}{9} + \frac{1681}{9} + \frac{16}{9} + \frac{289}{9}}{6}}
&= \sqrt{\frac{\frac{196 + 2704 + 256 + 1681 + 16 + 289}{9}}{6}}
&= \sqrt{\frac{\frac{5142}{9}}{6}}
&= \sqrt{\frac{857}{9}}
&= 9.758\ldots
## Round to 1 decimal place
\sigma &\approx 9.8
ANSWER: \text{Range} = 31, \quad \sigma = 9.8
